    "question": {
      ":question/id": "108cf678-1e16-5de6-b610-dca0fd54adf4",
      ":question/problem": "Find the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(-75^\\circ\\right)$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that*\n\n$$\n-75^\\circ=60^\\circ-135^\\circ.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x-y)=\\cos x\\cos y+\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(-75^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(60^\\circ-135^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(60^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(135^\\circ\\right)+\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(135^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\\n&=\\frac{- \\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
